{
  "$comment": [
    "Timing parity table (ARCHITECTURE §4.13, §8.8; PRD §4.3.2, §4.3.3, §4.3.6): request counting for the latency allowance, AC-DLY-23, and the honest-play thresholds of AC-DLY-25 with the missing-report flag.",
    "Replayed by Vitest against src/engine/scoring/ranking.ts (countRequests, effectiveRoundMs, totalRunMs) and percentile.ts (honestPlayFlags), and from SQL-5 by the generated timing tests.",
    "config holds the shared values the rows assume; the engine test checks them against src/config/shared.json (latencyAllowanceMs, roundCapMs, honestPlayHiddenMs, tooFastMs), so a change there fails until this table follows.",
    "requests: the calls one round made, as the server saw them. The round's opening call counts once (begin_round, or for round 0 the start call that opened it); every accepted state-changing action counts (a wrong guess, Next clue, a pick, an encore lock-in, a choice answer, and the resolving one); refused calls (invalid_entity, already_guessed, stale, rate_limited), replays of a known key and repeated begin_round calls never count.",
    "rounds: effective time = max(serverMs - 400 × requests, clientMs), never below 0, capped at 15 minutes. totals: the sum over a run's rounds; a voided round adds nothing.",
    "honestPlay: a run's rounds (hiddenMs is the largest hidden time the round reported, null when an action arrived without a report; solve is how a Mystery was solved and how long after its clue, or for a pick after the options), the expert-slot dwell, the zone change of memo §14.1 and low trust. flags is the stored bitmask: 1 hidden, 2 expert slot, 4 too fast, 8 missing report, 16 zone change, 32 low trust. The too-fast check counts a typed solve at too_fast_ms itself (within 1.5 s); hidden play flags at honest_play_hidden_ms or more; the expert check needs a dwell strictly above its limit."
  ],
  "config": {
    "latencyAllowanceMs": 400,
    "roundCapMs": 900000,
    "honestPlayHiddenMs": 5000,
    "tooFastMs": 1500
  },
  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "start-round-0",
      "title": "round 0 counts the start call that opened it, plus its answer",
      "calls": ["start", "accepted"],
      "requests": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "begin-and-actions",
      "title": "begin_round, a wrong guess, Next clue and the solve make 4",
      "calls": ["begin_round", "accepted", "accepted", "accepted"],
      "requests": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "refused",
      "title": "an unknown entity and a repeated guess consume nothing and count nothing",
      "calls": ["begin_round", "invalid_entity", "already_guessed", "accepted"],
      "requests": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "stale-rate-limited",
      "title": "stale and rate-limited calls never count",
      "calls": ["begin_round", "stale", "rate_limited", "accepted"],
      "requests": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "replays",
      "title": "replays of a known key never count",
      "calls": ["begin_round", "accepted", "replay", "replay"],
      "requests": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "repeated-begin",
      "title": "a repeated begin_round never counts",
      "calls": ["begin_round", "begin_round", "begin_round", "accepted"],
      "requests": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "encore-lock-in",
      "title": "an Encore: begin_round and the lock-in",
      "calls": ["begin_round", "accepted"],
      "requests": 2
    }
  ],
